About StarRez

StarRez is the global leader in student housing software, providing innovative solutions for on and off-campus housing management, resident wellness and experience, and revenue generation. Trusted by 1,400+ clients across 25+ countries, StarRez supports more than 4 million beds annually with its user-friendly, all-in-one platform, delivering seamless experiences for students and administrators. With offices in the United States, Australia, the UK, and India, StarRez blends the robust capabilities of a global organization with the personalized care and service of a trusted partner.

The Role &nbsp;

We are seeking a Director of Customer Success to lead and continue developing our global Customer Success team across StarRez, College Pads, and the Customer Success teams of businesses we acquire in the future. In this role you will lead across all our platforms and regions, holding us to our goal of being customer obsessed so that our customers are happy and using their full product suite. Alongside that, you will take a heavy focus on the College Pads renewal process and customer retention. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Role Specifics &nbsp;

• Work Location: Remote (US). This is a US-based role.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Travel: Up to 15% (The percentage of travel is an estimation and could vary up or down based on business needs.) &nbsp;

• Reporting Structure: This role reports to the VP, Global Customer Success. &nbsp;

What You Will Own &nbsp;

• Lead, coach and develop the global Customer Success team across StarRez and College Pads, building a structure that works across regions, time zones and platforms. &nbsp;

• Own retention and renewal outcomes, including the College Pads renewal process end to end, forecasting accuracy and the plays that reduce churn risk. &nbsp;

• Drive product adoption and utilization across the customer base, so institutions realize the full value of what they have bought, including proactive best-practice guidance. &nbsp;

• Own executive-level customer relationships and be the accountable leader on complex escalations, working closely with Support, Services and Account Management to resolve them. &nbsp;

• Review and improve our Customer Success operating model, including segmentation, health scoring, tooling and reporting, and make clear recommendations for improvements. &nbsp;

• Build the reporting layer that leadership relies on, producing Salesforce-based reporting and analysis for SLT and Board audiences. &nbsp;

• Partner cross-functionally with Services, Support, Renewals, Account Management, Product, Legal and Finance, so customers experience one joined-up company rather than a set of departments. &nbsp;

• Integrate Customer Success teams from acquired businesses into a single way of working. &nbsp;

Required Qualifications &nbsp;

• 5+ years' experience leading Customer Success teams in a SaaS environment. &nbsp;

• Experience with Digital and Scaled Customer Success &nbsp;

• Experience leading people management, with team members based in more than one country or region. &nbsp;

• Demonstrated ownership of retention, renewal or utilization outcomes. &nbsp;

• Track record of managing and resolving complex escalations, including direct engagement with customer executives. &nbsp;

• Strong Salesforce skills, including building and interpreting reporting for senior audiences. &nbsp;

• Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the credibility to hold a room with both a customer executive and an internal leadership team. &nbsp;

• Evidence of improving process, tooling or ways of working rather than simply operating what already exists. &nbsp;

• Based in the United States and able to work in US business hours. &nbsp;

Preferred Qualifications &nbsp;

• Experience working with higher education institutions, or an understanding of how university housing and residential life operate. &nbsp;

• Experience with renewals at scale, including forecasting and commercial negotiation. &nbsp;

Quality Area Manager

The Quality Area Manager will lead our QA and Sanitation teams to ensure Good Manufacturing Practices (GMPs) and sanitation meet our high-quality standards to provide the best service to our customers.&nbsp;

You will…&nbsp;

• Respectfully communicate with all co-workers. Ensure effective employee relations with all departments in the facility.

• Provide employee instructions to provide advice on how to properly perform their task (QA checks, cleaning equipment, expectations, etc.).

• Respectfully support and follow direction from all managers about line product integrity

• Work towards continuous improvement in all areas. Ensure all actions better the business of HelloFresh and do not break any company policies.

• Maintaining accurate documentation regarding GMPs, HACCP, processing analysis and environmental monitoring&nbsp;

• Coach QA &amp; Sanitation employees to follow company policies and procedures

• Train new employees on standard operating procedures

• Performs duties of workers supervised, as needed

• Ensure that the daily workload is equally distributed based priority and ability&nbsp;

• Reports defective materials or questionable conditions QA Manager

• Follows prescribed safety policies and regulations

• Completes tasks as directed with minimum supervision

• Occasionally required to inspect products or surfaces using tools such as thermometer, gas analyzers, food scales, gas analyzer, etc., as needed

• Update quality numbers in the computer system; must be able to use a computer and type/data entry using computer programs (Microsoft Office, Google Sheets)

• Report food safety and quality problems to personnel with authority to initiate action

• Report on any discrepancies pertaining to current week ingredients or packaging&nbsp;

Supervisory Responsibility&nbsp;

• This position provides guidance to employees by coordinating work and resolving problems. The FSQA Supervisor’s performance is evaluated by their leadership of the QA employees, productivity and prioritization of their designated team, quality/quantity of information reported each shift, and ability to guide employee performance on the team.&nbsp;

Work Environment&nbsp;

• While performing the duties of this job, the employee is in a manufacturing and assembly environment and is regularly exposed to cool and/or cold temperatures (30°F - 40°F). The employee is frequently exposed to fumes or airborne particles, moving mechanical parts and vibration. The noise level in the work environment and job sites can be loud.&nbsp;

Physical Demands&nbsp;

• While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand, walk, stoop, reach and lift for a minimum of 10 hours with or without reasonable accommodation. The employee is required to use hands to finger, handle, or feel objects and/or tools. The employee is required to talk or hear with or without reasonable accommodation. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and peripheral vision.&nbsp;

Position Type/Expected Hours of Work&nbsp;

• This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are varied according to shift. There are occasions where overtime is required based upon operational needs. The FSQA Supervisor is expected to work the hours it takes to finish assignments each day.&nbsp;

